{
    "_comment": [
        "Every *Continuation renderer name the YouTube TV app registers in its own",
        "renderer table, taken verbatim from the shipped kabuki bundle (main.js,",
        "the `new _.S(\"...\")` declarations). Captured rather than invented: the",
        "whole point is that this list is the app's, not ours.",
        "",
        "A continuation that carries shelves or tiles has to be routed through",
        "processShelves, or everything the mod does to a tile silently stops",
        "applying to content that arrives that way.",
        "",
        "`payloads` holds one real response envelope per content-carrying",
        "continuation, reduced to the shape the routing reads. They exist so the",
        "harness can EVALUATE the expression adblock.ts passes to processShelves and",
        "the per-item passes, rather than only checking that the call is written: a",
        "route can be present and inert, and the name-level checks above cannot tell",
        "the difference."
    ],
    "names": [
        "sectionListContinuation",
        "horizontalListContinuation",
        "gridContinuation",
        "tvSurfaceContentContinuation",
        "itemSectionContinuation",
        "reloadContinuation",
        "nextContinuation",
        "genericPromoContinuation"
    ],
